#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Step 06 Settle: the exchange's settlement object is on the rail, final, banded, and counted honestly.

Usage: 06-settle --population DIR --out DIR

On the rehearsal population (`"rail": "mock"`) the rail is the mock rail in
DIR/rail/ (population/rehearsal/rail/README.md): its declaration (rail.json,
naming the rail's TEST key) and its public ledger (ledger.jsonl, the settlement
objects the rail issued, in order). The exchange is DIR/step06/exchange.json;
it carries the settlement by reference only, `settlement_ref: {rail,
settlement_id}`, never a copy. Each node's disclosure, DIR/step06/disclosure-<node>.json,
is the settlement count the node states for the rail, signed with its key.
DIR/step06/controllers.json maps node keys to their controllers.

The step copies those files into its out directory and decides on the copies
alone (the proof bytes):
- ledger: every line passes the rail adapter's form, signature and id checks
  (population/rehearsal/rail/mock_rail.py, shaped like evidencebook's
  adapters), sequences run 1..n, and no settlement id repeats;
- reference: the exchange's settlement_ref names this rail and exactly one
  ledger line, and the exchange carries nothing else of the settlement;
- adapter, finality, rail_fee, band: the adapter's reports on that line, each
  PASS; the band is derived from the object's amount and currency;
- exchange_match: the object's exchange id, payer, payee, currency and amount
  are the exchange's;
- ledger_count:<node>: the disclosure verifies under the node's key, and its
  count is the ledger's count of final settlements the node is a party to.
PASS when all hold, FAIL when any does not. volume.json is the filtered and
raw settlement counts over the ledger (the status page's number): raw counts
the final settlements; filtered keeps those on a fee-paying rail whose payer
and payee are declared under different controllers.

On the live population no rail is verified: the lab nodes record their
wallets' reports of Lightning payments (capsules plugin settlement legs and
payment.lifecycle.v1 observations in <data_dir>/ledger/capsules.jsonl), not
the rail's own settlement objects, and the lab has no rail. The pinned
Lightning adapter (capsules-plugin lightning-v0) reports on the node's own book
only. The step reads what each node recorded, lists it (recorded.json per
node), and is NOT_CHECKED on that gap (evidence-network/loop#243).

Where a settlement observation carries the payment's preimage, the step checks
finality itself. The host passes the preimage with mesh-llm#2744 (open; the lab
build carries it) and the lexe-wallet-plugin#7 wallet build. The preimage must
be 32 bytes of lowercase hex with sha256(preimage) == payment_hash. Only a
payer observation's preimage proves a payment; the provider holds its preimage
before it is paid. recorded.json keeps the check's outcome, never the
preimage. A preimage that is malformed or does not hash to its payment hash is
a FAIL, on either side: the node recorded a settlement whose own preimage does
not match it. With every recorded hash proven by a payer's preimage the
finality gap closes, but the step stays NOT_CHECKED on the rail's settlement
object by reference. A node with nothing recorded, or no readable data_dir, is
NOT_CHECKED too. The step never pays: it moves no money with or without
LOOP_LIVE_SPEND, and says so in detail.

Exit 0 once the finding is written, whatever the result; non-zero when the
step itself broke (unreadable population, no rail files).
"""
